#!/bin/sh
#
# commfailure / commok for the apcupsd network clients f1-f3 -- managed by
# gonf (freebsd_apcupsd_client_events, gonf/freebsd/apcupsd.go).
#
# The stock scripts mail root on every lost/restored event. A client loses its
# UPS feed whenever f0 is down: at every nightly power-off and morning
# power-on (the clients' apcupsd polls before f0's has started) and on every
# f0 reboot. That produced ~900 mails on f2 and no real finding, so the
# clients stay quiet: apcupsd itself still records the event in syslog and
# /var/log/apcupsd.events. f0 keeps the stock (mailing) scripts, where a lost
# USB link to the UPS is a real problem.
#
# Exit 99 tells apccontrol to skip its default action (a wall(1) broadcast).
exit 99
